SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers only what the 1.6 port added:

  - the corrections to the defs: wildness moved from a race property to the
    Wildness stat on both penguins, and the mod's redeclarations of Core's
    abstract egg bases removed - two deleted outright, the third kept under a
    name of its own, Penguins_EggFertBase
  - the rewritten Giddy-Up patch, which targets Giddy-Up 2's GiddyUp.Drawing-
    Offset on the emperor penguin instead of a class that no longer exists on
    a defName that never existed, and guards on one of Giddy-Up's own defs
    instead of on its display name
  - the replacement of the source mod's four sound defs with Core's own
    waterfowl - see below for why they are not here
  - the corrected labels, and the renaming of the emperor penguin's pack
    texture to the facing suffix the game actually reads
  - the French translation
  - the packaging and the documentation

IT DOES NOT COVER THE ORIGINAL MOD. The two penguins, their stats, their eggs
and their ten textures are Peso penguin's work, reused here:

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3477589277

They never declared a licence for it, so none is granted here and none can be.
It is redistributed under the usual practice for abandoned mods - explicit
credit, a link to the original, and removal on request. About/Preview.png is
theirs as it stands.

If Peso penguin asks for this to be taken down, it comes down. Immediately,
and without discussion.


ONE THING WAS DELIBERATELY LEFT BEHIND

The source mod shipped four sound files and four SoundDefs named
AEXP_Pawn_Penguin_*. Those are Vanilla Animals Expanded's: the defNames are
its own, and the .ogg files are byte-identical to its. Vanilla Animals
Expanded is alive, declares 1.6, and is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 - a named licence
with No Derivatives - so none of it is redistributed here, and no permission
over it is granted or implied by anything above. The penguins use Core's
Pawn_Duck_* and Pawn_Goose_* instead.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was changed.
